{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730408Z","id":"b8aab2610f59a590ca413b5cd9fd9ca479849a735320deea10160a2155467fa0","body":{"detail":"ClaxTools here gets no upgrade-hold probe (with_upgrade_hold is never called), so status over the daemon-served MCP endpoint never carries upgrade_held (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1285-1290). The shim, the CLI and Pi report it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"a25bc2b65e3c49b01b8458ea877c1bfa039ac0f80052a5a7d7e7d1450f8652e6"},"summary":"The daemon's own /mcp status does not report upgrade_held","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730968Z","id":"35baa8b0f265d09f864dd92ddd5918392c44ca0074f4c8ca9c750c6c90dfb0d8","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":331},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:29:45.207526Z","id":"883584b3ad6905461c2178a9d2f613cbafef211ee0535b8d509519da776a6fe0","body":{"detail":"ClaxTools here gets no upgrade-hold probe (with_upgrade_hold is never called), so status over the daemon-served MCP endpoint never carries upgrade_held (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1285-1290). The shim, the CLI and Pi report it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"bf718c5220791a2ab835891ca9f59556af6e625096c9dfa63042bde16d094a30"},"summary":"The daemon's own /mcp status does not report upgrade_held","supersedes":"b8aab2610f59a590ca413b5cd9fd9ca479849a735320deea10160a2155467fa0","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:29:45.207627Z","id":"3f206f41a6e6622d8ee312c392795dff19fa491a82e5981aba47e01580a9e799","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":346},"end":{"line":348},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"35baa8b0f265d09f864dd92ddd5918392c44ca0074f4c8ca9c750c6c90dfb0d8","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.661400Z","id":"c20422c881c5477cc8c3cad8c4ba4fa548a42217e77edaa703fdb7ff38926c3d","body":{"detail":"for_asker() sets question.artifact.title to null for Caller::PersonAgent whatever its approvals: the title is an author field (spec §8.2) and no Visibility exists yet. The owner's GET /api/questions and GET /api/questions/{qid} leave out questions of sessions with a person (store questions.rs owners!()), but crate::inbox::views still renders them as items of the owner's inbox (spec §18 wants the per-person inbox).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"95fe0b615c046cbaa45b6cd1d490d59fcff730299fe894d98ab591a843574543"},"suggested_fix":"Replace for_asker with the visibility filter when questions are filtered, and scope the inbox's question items per person (migration 25's per-person inbox).","summary":"A person's agent's question view nulls the artifact title instead of filtering it, and its questions still reach the owner's inbox","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.661648Z","id":"5f9d0c3719de303c1d4fa01a79067f54bcf54f066ef37945baaa6859804ccde8","body":{"detail":"Handlers used to test has_token(); they now match Caller::Owner { .. } | Caller::OwnerAgent { .. } (sees_sessions here, may_act_as_agent in routes/threads.rs:97). Caller::Owner { browser: true } is the same for an owner-cookie request with or without Authorization, so a cookie-only owner browser now gets owner_session_id and session_id fields, clip_path, and reopens or deletes threads without a display name. The golden (agent outputs) is unchanged; spec §19 lists the single-owner changes allowed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":264},"content_hash":"42d94c9021c52275c4f0fed69144d8ebf1256cb93d4e433d48c7ebe76eb4e5d1"},"suggested_fix":"If the shell always sends the token, nothing changes; otherwise carry 'token presented' on Caller::Owner, or confirm this as one of spec §19's changes.","summary":"An owner browser without the token now counts as holding it for session IDs, clip paths and naming-free reopen and delete","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.661875Z","id":"cca46f70442d60b2e4f8aa28b8770c585f21e7568aad38e1e0523415e567ed09","body":{"detail":"author(st, &who) reads the viewer from Identity; for a Clax-Grant request Identity has no token or cookie, so a person's agent's new thread or viewer comment would be stored with author_public_id None (*unconnected). The routes are Filtered and answer a person's agent 503 not_yet until their filter is live, so nothing reaches this today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":413},"end":{"line":413},"content_hash":"6f454b38ce15c8406225a3dc6f372035a2fc1b9cfd6cd1f0ed4745a1e42acbd6"},"suggested_fix":"Attribute a person's agent's writes to its person and session (as AUTHOR_AGENT with via_session_id) before ThreadsCreate and ThreadComment join agent::FILTERED_LIVE.","summary":"A thread or comment a person's agent writes is attributed through Identity, which makes it anonymous","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.662289Z","id":"2b60c45840e14af3c85c7654b59d52fd1a0d9d04870fd80070765919a17ca139","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1273},"end":{"line":1289},"content_hash":"4cb1fe9c2f23e827cfe65137e29b2bdf9ec189af81cd7552c358da87cb9c462a"},"suggested_fix":"Build every author-bearing view through named functions (artifact_view, version_view, doc_view, working_view, comment_view) as the filter lands, and keep this list to those names.","summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:27:15.662516Z","id":"425281edaf48edda6779e6e5024f24ded118ed103d17dffddfad761e4fb747d4","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1627},"end":{"line":1653},"content_hash":"83ed7864ba2897d0ff8421cfe185f069945dfbf2b21b7f774ccc58438abe14d5"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:52:59.949688Z","id":"bc65306f1ff4cad943f3cf43ebf3917faf1f9980f6ab900fd96b57c5abfdf894","body":{"detail":"lookup with the token lists viewers by name; the not_for_agents rule names person views and /api/people*. Names are not filtered (spec section 21.9), so this may be intended; no record says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"fdef32ef55ec060aeebfe4fd3b77d7814bf6706887dea024f0f20ef0a60067d3"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: refuse_agents() here, or record that names are not a person view.","summary":"The viewer name search serves the owner's agents","tags":["review","task-6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:53:00.002015Z","id":"f58112a5282ca4d26a7acd7758b5d6ded066572274d348275d83b35dee3a3d9f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:428c611","summary":"Fixed: Agent::holds_token() (the daemon token alone) now decides session IDs, clip paths and the name check (routes/artifacts.rs, routes/threads.rs may_act_as_agent). Test api_canary::the_owners_cookie_alone_is_not_the_token passes; with holds_token() widened to Caller::Owner it fails.","supersedes":"5f9d0c3719de303c1d4fa01a79067f54bcf54f066ef37945baaa6859804ccde8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970234Z","id":"c5595c22e7fafbf59719371cde3020e684786a794501fdcd325869c5c05fefb9","body":{"detail":"author(st, &who) reads the viewer from Identity; for a Clax-Grant request Identity has no token or cookie, so a person's agent's new thread or viewer comment would be stored with author_public_id None (*unconnected). The routes are Filtered and answer a person's agent 503 not_yet until their filter is live, so nothing reaches this today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":520},"end":{"line":520},"content_hash":"6f454b38ce15c8406225a3dc6f372035a2fc1b9cfd6cd1f0ed4745a1e42acbd6"},"suggested_fix":"Attribute a person's agent's writes to its person and session (as AUTHOR_AGENT with via_session_id) before ThreadsCreate and ThreadComment join agent::FILTERED_LIVE.","summary":"A thread or comment a person's agent writes is attributed through Identity, which makes it anonymous","supersedes":"cca46f70442d60b2e4f8aa28b8770c585f21e7568aad38e1e0523415e567ed09","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970489Z","id":"bd6301a402ac7d7fbb6f04b75a0c875b289ee6167f0af811d68bd7d0b7a3260d","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1640},"end":{"line":1666},"content_hash":"83ed7864ba2897d0ff8421cfe185f069945dfbf2b21b7f774ccc58438abe14d5"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"425281edaf48edda6779e6e5024f24ded118ed103d17dffddfad761e4fb747d4","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970811Z","id":"4055a6f8cca3f3235a912b745deaa277c7a99ddfeee284a25843c847a4b1f21f","body":{"detail":"Spec §10 says sending to another person's agent (button, to, @name) stores the send and makes a routing request that its person approves; a send to an agent that may not read the artifact is 400 agent_cannot_read. named_agent_reaches only checks rights (and refuses live pages); a comment's @name to such an agent lists it in unresolved_mentions rather than failing the comment. Delivery to a person's agent is 503 not_yet until the feedback routes join agent::FILTERED_LIVE, so nothing reaches one today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":254},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"2f6f9f83cb96b2053f47df36762060ba5f55db77755bc5da57e3e4b355b18b25"},"suggested_fix":"When approval requests exist (spec §9.2), make @name to another person's agent a routing request like a send with to, and decide whether an unreadable target is unresolved or a separate field in the comment's answer.","summary":"@name to a person's agent makes no routing request: it sends when the agent's rights allow reading and watching the artifact, else reports the name unresolved","tags":["spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.971085Z","id":"12bc834768f3652b24d3ae4fe8e18ecc8ec1680362b55c2f079451833ce926f2","body":{"detail":"announce_new_thread returns the @names that reached no agent; threads::create and threads::comment put them in their answers, but live::create_thread discards them, so the extension cannot say an @name went nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":452},"end":{"line":453},"content_hash":"d616bfd5a1a1a480f8733a7c3467b538a639ad6eea8827c4f32a507f9d48cc9c"},"summary":"A live page's thread answer drops unresolved_mentions","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.971229Z","id":"b4bf1f08d4c561fd1512fcb8d8c99cf70ccc391bdbe1b4739980e5c82bfc1ad3","body":{"detail":"mint now refuses the owner's agents (not_for_agents). clax native-host builds its Client with channel::from_process, so if Chrome inherited CLAUDECODE, CODEX_* or PI_CODING_AGENT from a shell it was launched from, the native host marks itself an agent channel and pairing fails with 403.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"0a3ac3d0f6add4915352c4d6de1a82da7fc50c6e21fb44f0a2bb7bd80c378596"},"summary":"The native host cannot pair when Chrome was started from a harness's shell","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:55.332167Z","id":"2da84c9808d4ea68fc9560c9f7826c6a6d78a134c253a5d73ebb8a01c9b716a2","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1280},"end":{"line":1296},"content_hash":"4cb1fe9c2f23e827cfe65137e29b2bdf9ec189af81cd7552c358da87cb9c462a"},"suggested_fix":"Build every author-bearing view through named functions (artifact_view, version_view, doc_view, working_view, comment_view) as the filter lands, and keep this list to those names.","summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"2b60c45840e14af3c85c7654b59d52fd1a0d9d04870fd80070765919a17ca139","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.121417Z","id":"46b66c438abc789d07535844e30bd174eae3d7c86b7b129d11516320ca728eba","body":{"detail":"launch.sh execs `ensure-clax.sh exec native-host`, which exports CLAX_CHANNEL=agent (scripts/ensure-clax.sh:123-127). Inherited harness variables are a second path: Chrome started from LaunchServices (Dock, Finder, `open`) gets launchd's environment and inherits none, but Chromium launched by Playwright inherits the test runner's environment (CLAUDECODE=1 when an agent runs the e2e suite), and on Linux a browser started by xdg-open from an agent's shell or a daemon the agent started inherits it too. See the blocker on crates/clax-cli/src/commands/native_host.rs:151:161.","kind":"comment","references":"b4bf1f08d4c561fd1512fcb8d8c99cf70ccc391bdbe1b4739980e5c82bfc1ad3","summary":"Pairing fails on every install, not only when Chrome inherited a harness variable: the launcher itself sets CLAX_CHANNEL=agent","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.122092Z","id":"53fb2aa29244e7bbf63af637b5dbb4a290f786326c806723500aa7b221d50666","body":{"detail":"Names are unique only among live sessions (spec section 11), so when the owner's 'web' ends, a person's agent may PATCH its name to 'web' and the owner's next '@web' goes to it, moving the thread's untargeted rows with it (send_to_named). Until section 10's routing request lands, nothing tells the commenter. Task 14's routing request should name the person, and the thread answer could carry the reached agent's person.","kind":"comment","references":"4055a6f8cca3f3235a912b745deaa277c7a99ddfeee284a25843c847a4b1f21f","summary":"The answer to an @name does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:19.217929Z","id":"fe4cc7e23a1330d29919b8f6e59b7d3e4c976a34a1402dac6366eea1469f95e3","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. Nothing in the comment's answer names the agent or its person, and spec §10's routing request, which would, is not made yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":292},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"06daa4ae0ef0c442599343c9806d45c351cbd0676bbba21224ef6710a3447895"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:50.467773Z","id":"f51cf67b4248787c334981292ccc02f1a713d385f42bf2c2a532424de92c6660","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:868fdf4","summary":"Fixed in 868fdf4: native_host::pair mints through Client::owner_channel whatever its environment, and ensure-clax.sh exempts native-host. crates/clax-cli/tests/extension.rs the_installed_launcher_pairs_as_the_owner_under_a_harness_environment pairs through the installed launch.sh with CLAUDECODE=1 and CLAX_CHANNEL=agent (it fails with owner_channel removed); scripts/test-ensure-clax.sh checks the exemption; web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts 18 passed with CLAUDECODE=1 in the runner's environment. The remaining path (an owner's agent running clax native-host itself) is the waiver on crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:497:500.","supersedes":"b4bf1f08d4c561fd1512fcb8d8c99cf70ccc391bdbe1b4739980e5c82bfc1ad3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:22:00.597663Z","id":"fe25c4c98063afe51301915e4dbe71a0e7c16ceaa38e8180be6d4e4585356ed0","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1641},"end":{"line":1667},"content_hash":"83ed7864ba2897d0ff8421cfe185f069945dfbf2b21b7f774ccc58438abe14d5"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"bd6301a402ac7d7fbb6f04b75a0c875b289ee6167f0af811d68bd7d0b7a3260d","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619473Z","id":"ac364ac2059f0ee2dc92654f01f42a4582499a29ea0a9740237baf8f9f6b1516","body":{"detail":"ClaxTools here gets no upgrade-hold probe (with_upgrade_hold is never called), so status over the daemon-served MCP endpoint never carries upgrade_held (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1285-1290). The shim, the CLI and Pi report it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"bf718c5220791a2ab835891ca9f59556af6e625096c9dfa63042bde16d094a30"},"summary":"The daemon's own /mcp status does not report upgrade_held","supersedes":"883584b3ad6905461c2178a9d2f613cbafef211ee0535b8d509519da776a6fe0","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619624Z","id":"7523c83deb06ab9dc479c839ba6f5915a6b82c8d8fe409beca1377e4b5c36645","body":{"detail":"API JSON, the shell's pages and bundles, and the bridge are compressed (crate::http_cache::compression(), lines 261, 295, 305); wrapped pages and supporting files under /c/... (and on artifact origins) are not. On loopback this costs little; on a LAN view it lengthens link to first paint. Time to usable on a LAN link has not been measured before and after compression.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":382},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"0183f2fb51d019b241c6aa757c2c79ed154d83a9bb42a0d49c08d2390b131255"},"summary":"Published pages and their files go out uncompressed","supersedes":"3f206f41a6e6622d8ee312c392795dff19fa491a82e5981aba47e01580a9e799","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619748Z","id":"b06bed237f3b537af0f88836053b031be9043224da85365727412c2d8d40da46","body":{"detail":"for_asker() sets question.artifact.title to null for Caller::PersonAgent whatever its approvals: the title is an author field (spec §8.2) and no Visibility exists yet. The owner's GET /api/questions and GET /api/questions/{qid} leave out questions of sessions with a person (store questions.rs owners!()), but crate::inbox::views still renders them as items of the owner's inbox (spec §18 wants the per-person inbox).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"b532c1383250d597fa64b1cda0b14d94c3c2f0e35de1d852fec34ed13cc7ba69"},"suggested_fix":"Replace for_asker with the visibility filter when questions are filtered, and scope the inbox's question items per person (migration 25's per-person inbox).","summary":"A person's agent's question view nulls the artifact title instead of filtering it, and its questions still reach the owner's inbox","supersedes":"c20422c881c5477cc8c3cad8c4ba4fa548a42217e77edaa703fdb7ff38926c3d","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619882Z","id":"3bf940526e34b0fd1a6e732658e8e653c02e63b14e87ad6a8e61b3a2a523aae3","body":{"detail":"author(st, &who) reads the viewer from Identity; for a Clax-Grant request Identity has no token or cookie, so a person's agent's new thread or viewer comment would be stored with author_public_id None (*unconnected). The routes are Filtered and answer a person's agent 503 not_yet until their filter is live, so nothing reaches this today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":520},"end":{"line":520},"content_hash":"07bc579aa3d6c39071fe1fc44810958f2c325dcf43dea3e4644ce9c84ea27758"},"suggested_fix":"Attribute a person's agent's writes to its person and session (as AUTHOR_AGENT with via_session_id) before ThreadsCreate and ThreadComment join agent::FILTERED_LIVE.","summary":"A thread or comment a person's agent writes is attributed through Identity, which makes it anonymous","supersedes":"c5595c22e7fafbf59719371cde3020e684786a794501fdcd325869c5c05fefb9","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620011Z","id":"2258489355e69e74bc84e69888fea096ddd7bb2991eb66052ea5779821cd4225","body":{"detail":"Spec §10 says sending to another person's agent (button, to, @name) stores the send and makes a routing request that its person approves; a send to an agent that may not read the artifact is 400 agent_cannot_read. named_agent_reaches only checks rights (and refuses live pages); a comment's @name to such an agent lists it in unresolved_mentions rather than failing the comment. Delivery to a person's agent is 503 not_yet until the feedback routes join agent::FILTERED_LIVE, so nothing reaches one today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":254},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"15860d8f518a31f559dec4b3f1bdef653fbc2027d4c55e5c6558d41250d245d2"},"suggested_fix":"When approval requests exist (spec §9.2), make @name to another person's agent a routing request like a send with to, and decide whether an unreadable target is unresolved or a separate field in the comment's answer.","summary":"@name to a person's agent makes no routing request: it sends when the agent's rights allow reading and watching the artifact, else reports the name unresolved","supersedes":"4055a6f8cca3f3235a912b745deaa277c7a99ddfeee284a25843c847a4b1f21f","tags":["spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620159Z","id":"21254c3d3f666f2683916104e51ddbe215c6824b70094076a923d921b746f355","body":{"detail":"announce_new_thread returns the @names that reached no agent; threads::create and threads::comment put them in their answers, but live::create_thread discards them, so the extension cannot say an @name went nowhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":452},"end":{"line":453},"content_hash":"951ad5f5efc1832ae06efe1d11fb5641065e27f2b7f937c01e21d4e7863a0c5a"},"summary":"A live page's thread answer drops unresolved_mentions","supersedes":"12bc834768f3652b24d3ae4fe8e18ecc8ec1680362b55c2f079451833ce926f2","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620305Z","id":"279fa7ff6e009034cc996251bb6fd8b63fe261ce62e891fa50cfa33b9f314766","body":{"detail":"CONTENT_VIEWS and PEOPLE_VIEWS list the calls that build views in this codebase (thread_view(, with_owner(, list_versions(, doc_get(, working.for_artifact(, question_view(, inbox_views(, grant_view(, Sse::new(, ...). A handler that serialises an Artifact or a Version directly (json!({\"artifact\": a})) or calls a helper that does is not seen. MUST_REFUSE pins the routes spec §7.5 names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1240},"end":{"line":1256},"content_hash":"15b58d54d216c92b15b7e556791dbb98864326dd127b1d018b35223a0a61afa6"},"suggested_fix":"Build every author-bearing view through named functions (artifact_view, version_view, doc_view, working_view, comment_view) as the filter lands, and keep this list to those names.","summary":"The Own and not_for_agents guards recognise views by source text","supersedes":"2da84c9808d4ea68fc9560c9f7826c6a6d78a134c253a5d73ebb8a01c9b716a2","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620433Z","id":"393bc16d1befd9c1564927c1d0e452f20355dd3f08e380683b67f6f63feb02d4","body":{"detail":"Names are unique among live sessions only. When the owner's `web` ends, a person's agent may PATCH itself to `web`; the owner's next `@web` then reaches it (where its rights allow) and send_to_named moves the thread's untargeted rows to it. Nothing in the comment's answer names the agent or its person, and spec §10's routing request, which would, is not made yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":292},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"d2dc2d626b0b84978ec419e54713d3b4a62263bd38afcf8aebf3f3849cd7ff37"},"suggested_fix":"Name the reached agents and their persons in the comment's answer, and make §10's routing request for another person's agent.","summary":"An @name answer does not say whose agent it reached, and a person's agent may take an ended owner agent's name","supersedes":"fe4cc7e23a1330d29919b8f6e59b7d3e4c976a34a1402dac6366eea1469f95e3","tags":["spec:10","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620576Z","id":"7a293c3073fb3f9fd49db2b3318ddc28e337ebd14433cf0b6179ea4cc2a97256","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.6 allowlists two direct spawns. plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts also runs `<bin> --version` (binaryVersion) and `ensure-clax.sh` with no arguments (findBinary, which prints the binary's path). Neither reaches the daemon or the model's context, so the guard accepts them.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1601},"end":{"line":1627},"content_hash":"97f50ecd810399c4b5a68639bbfa6eb58bafe30c2dfd24e699d0f548022d2699"},"summary":"Pi may run the binary directly for --version, and the wrapper with no arguments, beside serve --json and status --json","supersedes":"fe25c4c98063afe51301915e4dbe71a0e7c16ceaa38e8180be6d4e4585356ed0","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:16.069318Z","id":"7249e30bf73fb1bd9dc61ff481d29b95847aaeea45c663e2fbcc75e291f98d58","body":{"detail":"POST /api/sessions/{id}/tool-calls (here) and POST /api/sessions/{id}/tool-call-ids (crates/clax-server/src/routes/sessions.rs:534:540) take DeniedToGrants and RequireToken, so a shim or Claude Code hook on another machine (a Clax-Grant caller) gets 403 forbidden when it reports a call. The events its requests make still carry the x-clax-call header's call (audit spec §5.2, amended 2026-10-10), so the call's name, argument hash and start time are kept; its end, outcome, produced list and harness call ID are not. Spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5 lists neither route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":379},"end":{"line":385},"content_hash":"e662e3e5e230ae2bbd36b754c7184d915e95a24ff1b77f4ef25b95d367e16b3c"},"suggested_fix":"Declare both as Own agent routes (need!(…, None, Own, DEFAULT_LIMIT), agent::ROUTES, agent::ROUTE_NEEDS, a §7.5 row), record the call as the session's agent (its actor already carries grant_id and person), and drop a report's artifact_id that names an artifact the grant may not read or a live page, so the call never lands in a path the agent cannot see.","summary":"A person's agents' tool calls are never recorded as tool.call or tool.call_id: the report routes refuse grants","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:16.069391Z","id":"ae067b6726e53a0c7e9e580511bd9737ad86a0ed1b64ced57e21234c55ccd788","body":{"detail":"The export holds every person's content unfiltered (titles, comment bodies, names), so the multi-person not_for_agents rule (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §7.5) refuses the owner's agents; the canary sweep (crates/clax-server/tests/api_canary.rs, no_canary_reaches_the_owners_agent_through_a_denied_route) found Mia's canaries in it before the refusal. On a single-owner install this takes the export away from an agent that ran it for the owner. The options are: keep the refusal; let owner agents export with --no-text --no-names (the redacted export holds no other person's text or names); or filter the export by visibility once the filter lands (Task 8).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":275},"end":{"line":282},"content_hash":"c999e8def53d154c4c3b3e4130701a6ba8fd9b6ed4134f44a7686b641ea38f24"},"summary":"clax toolpath export under a harness is refused (403 not_for_agents): only the CLI run by hand, or with CLAX_CHANNEL=owner, can export","tags":["merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:16.069462Z","id":"a2b6e191dc6cac2d78641134026793ad76606da49673b52f97a1a6dbd3d09df3","body":{"detail":"Audit spec §6.4 says a page watch Clax makes for a session rather than the session asking carries `cause` (scope or move). resolve_named gives a named live agent a direct watch under the commenter's audit context with Store::ensure_watch, which records watch.start {source: direct} with no cause, so the journal reads as if the agent watched the artifact itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":316},"end":{"line":316},"content_hash":"98e25bcd9cb452c8ac827ed8b38e60fd34b7539f5d0c83225bc42dc9baf3c5a6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `mention` cause (with the comment's ID) to audit spec §6.4 and record it here, as the scope and move causes are.","summary":"A watch @name makes for an agent is recorded as an ordinary watch.start: it carries no cause","tags":["merge","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259372Z","id":"45e409e64fbce6a95683f139b5754353db2950da018ac45789b2009373d1cc66","body":{"detail":"LAN viewers are *unconnected authors (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person M14): their comment bodies and names in the export are the same untrusted input for the owner's agents on a single-owner install as a person's are, and the owner can withdraw the *unconnected approval. So: (1) now, admit the owner's agents (OwnerAgent) to GET /api/toolpath/export with no_text and no_names forced (refuse an agent request that asks for text or names with 403 not_for_agents naming the flags), since the redacted export holds hashes in place of free text and no names; (2) with Task 8, filter the export per reader as the visibility filter does elsewhere (per-field placeholders for authors the reader's person has not approved) and drop the forced redaction. PersonAgent stays refused (owner only, audit spec section 8.3).","kind":"comment","references":"ae067b6726e53a0c7e9e580511bd9737ad86a0ed1b64ced57e21234c55ccd788","summary":"Recommendation: refuse only while people exist is not enough; give owner agents the redacted export now and a per-reader filtered export with Task 8","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259392Z","id":"942acc31df151b72ed8dafeaf1bdadee059e299988c185df01dd39a0f580da63","body":{"detail":"Today a grant reaches no content route (POST /api/artifacts and the rest answer 503 not_yet for a Clax-Grant caller), so a person's agent's calls produce almost nothing; the call's name, hash and start time still ride each event's x-clax-call. Once Task 8 opens the content routes, a call with no tool.call loses its end, outcome, produced list and harness call ID. Land the suggested Own routes in the task that opens the first content route to grants, with the produced list scoped to the reporting session.","kind":"comment","references":"7249e30bf73fb1bd9dc61ff481d29b95847aaeea45c663e2fbcc75e291f98d58","summary":"Deferring is right for now, but this must land before a person's agents can reach routes that make events","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259409Z","id":"f42947cd08b22b1aa6769f583298015bc37b8e8578996a27b8d30419f97f897e","body":{"detail":"The watch.start is under the commenter's audit context with the agent's session, so who caused it is kept; what is missing is that @name, not the agent, asked. A mention cause (with the comment's ID) fits audit spec section 6.4 beside scope and move; it belongs with the @name routing work (thread.take cause mention, multi-person spec section 20.2).","kind":"comment","references":"a2b6e191dc6cac2d78641134026793ad76606da49673b52f97a1a6dbd3d09df3","summary":"Deferring is right: the watch is recorded with the right actor and session, only its cause is missing","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
